    {
        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention silent\" data-user-id=\"130384\">Riccardo Brasca</span> <a href=\"#narrow/channel/287929-mathlib4/topic/Unprovable.20decreasing_by/near/590174338\">schrieb</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>I am not sure about all the details, but I guess that the recursive call happens inside <code>Pi.Lex</code>, so there variables are abstracted and in practice you are stuck.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>yes, Pi.Lex does the recursive call on some (ts1 i) and (ts2 i)</p>",
        "id": 590175220,
        "sender_full_name": "Moritz Roos",
        "timestamp": 1776855949
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>This behaviour of  <code>decreasing_by</code> can't be intended though?</p>",
        "id": 590175373,
        "sender_full_name": "Moritz Roos",
        "timestamp": 1776855995
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I don't know.</p>",
        "id": 590176081,
        "sender_full_name": "Riccardo Brasca",
        "timestamp": 1776856199
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention silent\" data-user-id=\"602461\">Moritz Roos</span> <a href=\"#narrow/channel/287929-mathlib4/topic/Unprovable.20decreasing_by/near/590175373\">said</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>This behaviour of  <code>decreasing_by</code> can't be intended though?</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>what would you rather it do</p>",
        "id": 590176172,
        "sender_full_name": "Aaron Liu",
        "timestamp": 1776856227
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>it's not gonna unfold <code>Pi.Lex</code> for you</p>",
        "id": 590176214,
        "sender_full_name": "Aaron Liu",
        "timestamp": 1776856237
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Maybe it is for some performance reason? Otherwise the unfolding may be very expensive.</p>",
        "id": 590176273,
        "sender_full_name": "Riccardo Brasca",
        "timestamp": 1776856256
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>This is quite the same issue like with recursion through <code>List.map</code>? You cannot tell from the type of <code>Pi.Lex</code> that it calls its arguments on something smaller?</p>\n<p>You can make it work automatically with a few helper definitions and <code>wf_preprocess</code> attributes, maybe.</p>",
        "id": 590177491,
        "sender_full_name": "Joachim Breitner",
        "timestamp": 1776856609
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention silent\" data-user-id=\"470149\">Joachim Breitner</span> <a href=\"#narrow/channel/287929-mathlib4/topic/Unprovable.20decreasing_by/near/590177491\">schrieb</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>You can make it work automatically with a few helper definitions and <code>wf_preprocess</code> attributes, maybe.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>Is there any examples to look at for this?</p>",
        "id": 590178015,
        "sender_full_name": "Moritz Roos",
        "timestamp": 1776856748
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I found a blog post by <span class=\"user-mention\" data-user-id=\"470149\">@Joachim Breitner</span> which was very useful <a href=\"https://www.joachim-breitner.de/blog/818-Seemingly_impossible_programs_in_Lean\">here</a>.</p>\n<p>Tagging a theorem containing the definition of <code>Pi.Lex</code> with <code>wf_preprocess</code> works:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">import</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Mathlib</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">inductive</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Term</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">F</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℕ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">where</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">var</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Term</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">F</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">func</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∀</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℕ</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">f</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">F</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">ts</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Fin</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Term</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">F</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"o\">),</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Term</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">F</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Term</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">size</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Term</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">F</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℕ</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">var</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">_</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">1</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">func</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">_</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">_</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ts</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">+</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Finset</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">univ</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">sum</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"k\">fun</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">ts</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">size</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n\n<span class=\"sd\">/-- This is basically the definition of `Pi.Lex` but as a theorem and tagget with `wf_preprocess`. -/</span>\n<span class=\"kd\">@[</span><span class=\"n\">wf_preprocess</span><span class=\"kd\">]</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">theorem</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">piLex_preprocess</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">ι</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">β</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ι</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"o\">}</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">r</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ι</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ι</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Prop</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">s</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∀</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"o\">},</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">β</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">β</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Prop</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">y</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∀</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">β</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">Pi</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Lex</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">r</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">s</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">y</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">↔</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"bp\">∃</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"bp\">∀</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">j</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">r</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">j</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">j</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">y</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">j</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∧</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">s</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">y</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">rfl</span>\n\n<span class=\"sd\">/--</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">trace: F : ℕ → Type u_1</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">α : Type u_2</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">n1 : ℕ</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">f1 : F n1</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">ts1 : Fin n1 → Term F α</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">n2 : ℕ</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">f2 : F n2</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">ts2 : Fin n2 → Term F α</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">hn : n1 = n2</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">i : Fin n1</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">⊢ (ts1 i).size + (Eq.rec (motive := fun x h =&gt; Fin x → Term F α) ts2 ⋯ i).size &lt;</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">    (func n1 f1 ts1).size + (func n2 f2 ts2).size</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">---</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">warning: declaration uses `sorry`</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">---</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">warning: declaration uses `sorry`</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">-/</span>\n<span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"n\">guard_msgs</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">in</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Term</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">kboLT</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">F</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℕ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">t1</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">t2</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Term</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">F</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Prop</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"k\">match</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">t1</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">t2</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">with</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">func</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n1</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">f1</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ts1</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">func</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n2</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">f2</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ts2</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"k\">if</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">hn</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n1</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n2</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">then</span>\n<span class=\"w\">      </span><span class=\"n\">Pi</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Lex</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"bp\">·</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">&lt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">·</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Term</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">kboLT</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">F</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ts1</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">hn</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">▸</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ts2</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"k\">else</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">False</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">_</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">_</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">False</span>\n<span class=\"n\">termination_by</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">t1</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">size</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">+</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">t2</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">size</span>\n<span class=\"n\">decreasing_by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">·</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">trace_state</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"gr\">sorry</span>\n</code></pre></div>",
        "id": 590184245,
        "sender_full_name": "Moritz Roos",
        "timestamp": 1776858510
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>im slightly confused why <code>attribute [wf_preprocess] Pi.Lex</code> didn't work though</p>",
        "id": 590184429,
        "sender_full_name": "Moritz Roos",
        "timestamp": 1776858561
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>And im completely terrified by this warning from the hover on the <code>wf_preprocess</code> attribute:</p>\n<p>Warning: These rewrites are only applied to the declaration for the purpose of the logical definition, <br>\nbut do not affect the compiled code. In particular they can cause a function definition that diverges <br>\nas compiled to be accepted without an explicit partial keyword, for example if they remove<br>\n irrelevant subterms or change the evaluation order by hiding terms under binders. <br>\nTherefore avoid tagging theorems with [wf_preprocess] unless they preserve also operational behavior.</p>",
        "id": 590184666,
        "sender_full_name": "Moritz Roos",
        "timestamp": 1776858624
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I don't understand what is written after <code>for example</code></p>",
        "id": 590185246,
        "sender_full_name": "Moritz Roos",
        "timestamp": 1776858761
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>And i want my function to be executable in real code and want it to be correct</p>",
        "id": 590185632,
        "sender_full_name": "Moritz Roos",
        "timestamp": 1776858859
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention silent\" data-user-id=\"602461\">Moritz Roos</span> <a href=\"#narrow/channel/287929-mathlib4/topic/Unprovable.20decreasing_by/near/590185632\">schrieb</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>And i want my function to be executable in real code and want it to be correct</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>The above warning sounds like lean doesn't guarantee this as soon as anyone tags anything in my dependency chain with <code>wf_preprocess</code></p>",
        "id": 590186156,
        "sender_full_name": "Moritz Roos",
        "timestamp": 1776859012
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>(Partial) correctness isn't threatened, you merely cannot assume that because you proved “logical termination”, that your compiled program also actually terminates.</p>",
        "id": 590186990,
        "sender_full_name": "Joachim Breitner",
        "timestamp": 1776859217
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Imagine <code>f n</code> is defined by <code>have _ := f n; …</code>. It is possible to prove that this is logically terminating (by removing the unused let), but the compiler may or may not do something similar, so the compiled code could just loop.</p>",
        "id": 590187503,
        "sender_full_name": "Joachim Breitner",
        "timestamp": 1776859343
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Oh, so lean already doesn't guarantee compiled code termination from logical termination for completely unrelated reasons already?<br>\nAnd do we have any way at all to ensure termination of  the compiled code (when assuming the compiler to be correct in some way)?</p>",
        "id": 590189616,
        "sender_full_name": "Moritz Roos",
        "timestamp": 1776859818
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>The waters are a bit muddy. For example, <code>partial</code> functions can be used just fine else, so knowing whether something should terminate is certainly not a on-your-nose thing. And of course every <code>implemented_by</code> becomes relevant.</p>\n<p>For structural and well-founded recursion we are optimistic that termination proofs imply that the program terminates, but this is not a formal guarantee (in the rigorous sense that we have proofs for logical statements). For example we believe that the <code>wf_preprocess</code> annotations in the standard library are fine. But again, not a guarantee that is that strong.</p>\n<p>Finally, I argue that this is less a problem in practice than it may seem, by  a reduction argument: a user who think they strongly care about about termination probably actually cares about “termination in practice in reasonable bounds”, because practically non-termination, and termination by the time the sun swallows the earth are equivalent. So if you care about the first, you care about the second, and at that point a <code>termination_by</code> is insufficient and you really need different approaches to prove computational bounds and things like that (which is not really possible with Lean like that, unfortunately).</p>\n<p>Not a happy argument, but an argument nevertheless :)</p>",
        "id": 590191045,
        "sender_full_name": "Joachim Breitner",
        "timestamp": 1776860140
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>hm i see :/</p>",
        "id": 590192469,
        "sender_full_name": "Moritz Roos",
        "timestamp": 1776860507
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention silent\" data-user-id=\"602461\">Moritz Roos</span> <a href=\"#narrow/channel/287929-mathlib4/topic/Unprovable.20decreasing_by/near/590184429\">schrieb</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>im slightly confused why <code>attribute [wf_preprocess] Pi.Lex</code> didn't work though</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>I guess tagging a \"definition but as a theorem\" theorem like i did above should be pretty safe right?</p>",
        "id": 590192700,
        "sender_full_name": "Moritz Roos",
        "timestamp": 1776860559
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Any reason for why tagging the def doesn't work?</p>",
        "id": 590192884,
        "sender_full_name": "Moritz Roos",
        "timestamp": 1776860605
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Not really pretty safe :-D</p>\n<p>Imagine you tag <code>Function.const</code>; that will remove the unused argument from the body, and thus may remove “bad” recursive calls there.</p>",
        "id": 590193048,
        "sender_full_name": "Joachim Breitner",
        "timestamp": 1776860647
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention silent\" data-user-id=\"602461\">Moritz Roos</span> <a href=\"#narrow/channel/287929-mathlib4/topic/Unprovable.20decreasing_by/near/590192884\">schrieb</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Any reason for why tagging the def doesn't work?</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>I am unsure. I configured the <code>simp</code> applying the <code>wf_preprocess</code> to be rather conservative (maybe no beta-reduction), that may prevent function unfolding.</p>",
        "id": 590193174,
        "sender_full_name": "Joachim Breitner",
        "timestamp": 1776860684
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention silent\" data-user-id=\"470149\">Joachim Breitner</span> <a href=\"#narrow/channel/287929-mathlib4/topic/Unprovable.20decreasing_by/near/590193048\">schrieb</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Not really pretty safe :-D</p>\n<p>Imagine you tag <code>Function.const</code>; that will remove the unused argument from the body, and thus may remove “bad” recursive calls there.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>Because the compiled code for <code>Function.const</code> will probably still evaluate the input and might loop in this evaluation?</p>",
        "id": 590193806,
        "sender_full_name": "Moritz Roos",
        "timestamp": 1776860856
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>In general, yes. Maybe <code>Function.const</code> gets inlined, maybe the compiler will do some optimizations. So in practice you may be fine. But that’s not a formal guarantee.</p>",
